cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hKCC: Key Characteristics of Human Carcinogens"
message: "If you use this dataset or software, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Data Analysis Team, KaziLab.se"
    email: hkcc@kazilab.se
abstract: >-
  An open, versioned database mapping carcinogenic agents to the ten key
  characteristics of carcinogens, alongside five candidate cross-cutting
  mechanistic domains that qualify an observation without being scored
  themselves. Evidence scores are derived from published IARC Monograph
  analyses by documented, deterministic rules, and each score records the
  derivation that produced it. Covers the Volume 100 Group 1 re-review
  (Krewski et al. 2019) and Volumes 112-130 (Rusyn et al. 2024). The 0-4 scale
  is ordinal and the two sources are not interchangeable; see
  docs/KCC_EVIDENCE_RULES.md before comparing scores. Data are licensed
  CC-BY-4.0; the accompanying software is MIT.
keywords:
  - carcinogenesis
  - key characteristics of carcinogens
  - IARC Monographs
  - mechanistic toxicology
  - cancer hazard identification
# This entry cites the dataset (type: dataset above), so the licence is the
# data licence. The software in the same repository is MIT — see LICENSE.
license: CC-BY-4.0
